      "text": "Whistleblowers claim that the U.S. government is operating a classified UFO crash retrieval and reverse engineering program. The Pentagon’s official UFO office (@DoD_AARO) says it investigated and found no evidence of any secret UFO programs. Are they telling the truth? Here’s a chronological timeline of 100 examples where U.S. defense and intelligence agencies lied to Congress and the public.\n\n2021: The Pentagon said a drone strike in Kabul killed ISIS terrorists, it actually killed ten civilians including seven children.\n\n2019: Officials concealed the fact that U.S. bombs killed dozens of civilians in Baghuz Syria.\n\n2018: The Pentagon denied deep involvement in the Saudi-led war in Yemen, records later proved it refueled and coordinated airstrikes.\n\n2017: They claimed precision in Mosul operations, but U.S. bombs destroyed entire neighborhoods and killed hundreds.\n\n2016: Leaders said there were “no boots on the ground” in Syria, U.S. troops were already fighting there.\n\n2015: The Pentagon said a hospital in Kunduz Afghanistan was hit by mistake, evidence showed repeated targeting calls during the attack.\n\n2014: They reported low civilian casualties in the ISIS war, later data proved thousands had died.\n\n2013: Defense officials said surveillance targeted foreigners, the NSA was spying on Americans too.\n\n2012: The Pentagon denied drone strikes killed civilians in Pakistan and Yemen, its own memos confirmed civilian deaths.\n\n2011: Officials said the Libya mission was to protect civilians, it was a covert regime-change war.\n\n2010: They claimed transparency in Iraq, but withheld reports documenting tens of thousands of civilian deaths.\n\n2009: Generals told the public the Afghanistan surge was succeeding, internal reviews admitted the opposite.\n\n2007: The Pentagon said civilian casualties in Iraq were decreasing, leaked numbers showed increases.\n\n2006: They called the Haditha killings a firefight, investigations proved U.S. Marines executed civilians.\n\n2005: Officials denied any torture by U.S. forces, classified files proved widespread abuse.\n\n2004: The Pentagon blamed “a few bad apples” for Abu Ghraib, torture was ordered through command channels.\n\n2004: They denied using banned munitions in Fallujah, evidence showed white phosphorus was used on civilians.\n\n2004: The Jessica Lynch “rescue” was staged, officials fabricated her hero story for propaganda.\n\n2004: They told Pat Tillman’s family he died heroically in combat, it was friendly fire deliberately covered up.\n\n2003: The Pentagon insisted Iraq had active weapons of mass destruction, none existed.\n\n2003: Officials said “shock and awe” bombing was surgical, it leveled cities and killed thousands.\n\n2002: They denied running secret prisons, black-site torture was later confirmed.\n\n2002: Officials said detainees in Bagram were treated humanely, two were beaten to death.\n\n2001: The Pentagon told Congress Afghanistan would be a short limited war, it lasted twenty years.\n\n2001: They said the U.S. was not spying on its citizens, warrantless surveillance began immediately after 9/11.\n\n1999: Officials claimed NATO bombs in Kosovo were precise, hundreds of civilians were killed.\n\n1996: They denied chemical exposure during weapons tests on U.S. troops, later declassified reports proved exposure.\n\n1995: The Pentagon dismissed Gulf War Illness as psychological, toxic exposures were later documented.\n\n1994: Officials said the Haiti mission was peacekeeping, it was a military occupation.\n\n1993: They described Somalia as humanitarian aid, it was a combat mission that ended in Black Hawk Down.\n\n1991: The Pentagon denied U.S. troops were exposed to sarin gas at Khamisiyah, sensors showed contamination.\n\n1991: They called Gulf War bombing “surgical,” civilian infrastructure was systematically destroyed.\n\n1990: Officials said Panama’s invasion was to arrest one man, thousands of civilians were killed.\n\n1989: The Pentagon denied abuses at Philippine bases, later testimony revealed systemic crimes.\n\n1987: They claimed ignorance of Iran-Contra arms trafficking, Pentagon records showed involvement.\n\n1986: Officials said the Libya airstrikes hit only military targets, civilians were bombed.\n\n1985: They denied aiding Nicaraguan Contras, funding and logistics were traced back to DoD.\n\n1984: The Pentagon defended the School of the Americas, its graduates led death squads.\n\n1983: They said the Grenada invasion rescued students, it was planned before the crisis.\n\n1982: Officials denied supporting Salvadoran death squads, training and weapons came from the U.S.\n\n1981: They denied covert operations in Nicaragua, CIA and Pentagon documents proved otherwise.\n\n1979: NATO leaders minimized nuclear-deployment risks, Pentagon analyses warned of catastrophe.\n\n1976: They denied DoD links to illegal human testing, Army and CIA experiments were later exposed.\n\n1975: Officials said the Cambodia evacuation was orderly, chaos and abandonment were covered up.\n\n1973: The Pentagon said bombing halted to advance peace, raids continued in secret.\n\n1972: They claimed B-52 bombing was effective and limited, civilian areas were destroyed by thousands of tons of bombs.\n\n1971: The Pentagon Papers proved decades of lies about Vietnam.\n\n1971: Officials insisted Agent Orange was safe, it caused cancers and birth defects.\n\n1970: They said the U.S. respected Cambodia’s borders, American forces invaded that year.\n\n1969: The Pentagon denied a massacre at My Lai, soldiers had executed over 500 unarmed civilians.\n\n1969: Officials said Vietnamization was succeeding, U.S. intelligence knew South Vietnam could not survive withdrawal.\n\n1968: They released fake body counts to show victory, the numbers were fabricated.\n\n1968: They called the Tet Offensive an enemy defeat, it was a strategic disaster for U.S. forces.\n\n1967: The Pentagon denied civilian assassinations under the Phoenix Program, thousands were killed.\n\n1966: They said the U.S. was not bombing Laos, hundreds of thousands of bombs were dropped.\n\n1965: Officials claimed the Dominican Republic intervention was to protect Americans, it was to crush a democratic uprising.\n\n1964: They said North Vietnam attacked twice in the Gulf of Tonkin, the second attack never happened.\n\n1963: The Pentagon called U.S. forces in Vietnam “advisors,” they were leading combat missions.\n\n1962: Officials drafted plans for fake terrorist attacks called Operation Northwoods, to justify war with Cuba.\n\n1962: They told sailors Project SHAD tests were safe, the experiments used chemical and biological agents.\n\n1961: The Pentagon denied involvement in the Bay of Pigs invasion, it had helped plan and support it.\n\n1960: They said a U-2 plane was a weather aircraft, it was a spy plane shot down over the USSR.\n\n1959: They told troops nuclear tests were harmless, soldiers were exposed to lethal radiation.\n\n1958: They said the Lebanon deployment was peacekeeping, it was to secure a pro-U.S. regime.\n\n1957: Officials warned of a “missile gap” with the Soviets, internal data showed the U.S. was far ahead.\n\n1956: The Pentagon said atomic tests in the Pacific were safe, islanders were poisoned by fallout.\n\n1955: They denied human experimentation, Edgewood Arsenal tested nerve gas on soldiers.\n\n1954: They said the U.S. had no role in Guatemala’s coup, it was organized and backed by U.S. forces.\n\n1953: They denied abuse of North Korean POWs, evidence later showed widespread violations.\n\n1952: Officials said atomic field tests were controlled, soldiers were ordered to march through nuclear blasts.\n\n1951: They called the Korean War a “limited conflict,” casualties exceeded two million.\n\n1950: They said the North Korean invasion was a surprise, intelligence had warned weeks before.\n\n1949: They claimed NATO was defensive, secret plans already included nuclear first strikes.\n\n1948: Officials said the Berlin airlift carried only food, it also moved military supplies.\n\n1947: The Pentagon dismissed early UFO reports as weather balloons, internal files showed ongoing investigations.\n\n1947: They said Operation Paperclip brought harmless scientists, many were high-ranking Nazis.\n\n1946: Officials told sailors Bikini tests were safe, radiation killed and sickened participants.\n\n1945: They said atomic bomb tests posed no danger to troops, radiation victims were denied care.\n\n1945: They said only military targets were bombed in Japan, entire civilian cities were destroyed.\n\n1944: They said friendly-fire losses were minimal in Normandy, thousands were killed by U.S. fire.\n\n1943: Officials said Black pilots lacked skill, the Tuskegee Airmen proved them wrong in combat.\n\n1943: They told troops mustard gas drills were harmless, soldiers suffered burns and poisoning.\n\n1942: They claimed Japanese internment was for security, it was driven by racism and hysteria.\n\n1942: They said Manila and Corregidor fell after fierce defense, leaders had abandoned the troops.\n\n1941: They claimed Pearl Harbor was a complete surprise, intelligence warnings were ignored.\n\n1941: They said the Atlantic Charter kept the U.S. neutral, Roosevelt had already committed to war.\n\n1940: They told the public Lend-Lease was not military aid, it was preparation for U.S. entry into WWII.\n\n1939: Officials downplayed rearmament costs, military budgets exploded in secret.\n\n1937: They claimed compliance with chemical weapons bans, new stockpiles were being built.\n\n1935: They said war games were for defense, they were designed to justify larger budgets.\n\n1932: They blamed veterans for the Bonus Army violence, U.S. troops burned their camps.\n\n1918: They said troop movements did not spread influenza, the Army helped cause the pandemic.\n\n1917: They claimed WWI would be short and glorious, it became one of the deadliest wars in history.\n\n1899: They said the Philippine-American War was liberation, it was brutal colonial conquest.\n\n1864: They said prisoners were treated humanely, thousands died of neglect and starvation.\n\n1846: They claimed Mexico started the war, U.S. troops had invaded Mexican territory first.\n\n1812: They promised readiness for war with Britain, troops lacked weapons and supplies.\n\n1778: They said shortages were minor, soldiers starved through the winter at Valley Forge.\n\n1776: They claimed the Continental Army was strong and supplied, it was disorganized and underfed.\n\n1775: They told the colonies the war would be short and easy, it lasted eight years.\n\n@RepLuna @RepNancyMace @RepTimBurchett @RepBoebert @RepEricBurlison @RepEliCrane @RepBrandonGill @CongressMin @RepRobertGarcia @CongressmanRaja @RepSummerLee @RepJasmine @jahimes @RepMoskowitz @SpeakerJohnson @AGPamBondi @AAGDhillon @DAGToddBlanche @FBIDirectorKash @FBIDDBongino @SecWar @DNIGabbard @ODNIgov @TheJusticeDept @CivilRights",
